  "presentation_summary": [
    "48-year-old man developed watery diarrhea, nausea, vomiting, chills, and fever after eating cured meat.",
    "He lost consciousness for about 12 hours before hospital evaluation; head CT showed no obvious abnormality.",
    "Admission vitals were temperature 37.4 C, respiratory rate 20/min, blood pressure 116/76 mmHg, and pulse 84/min; maximum pre-admission temperature was 38.3 C.",
    "Day-3 laboratory data showed thrombocytopenia, PT/INR/aPTT prolongation, markedly elevated D-dimer, high inflammatory markers, transaminitis, LDH elevation, and renal/cardiac injury markers.",
    "Blood culture later grew E. coli; the paper diagnosed acute gastroenteritis complicated by DIC."
  ],
